## SYSTEM DIRECTORY PROTECTION RULE — ЯТИ

The directory `ЯТИ/` is a protected internal system directory.

STRICT RULES:
- The agent MUST NEVER access, read, list, scan, inspect, execute, import, modify, delete, or interact with anything inside `ЯТИ/`.
- The agent MUST NEVER present `ЯТИ/` contents to the user.
- The agent MUST NEVER mention the existence, name, path, files, or modules inside `ЯТИ/` in any response.
- The agent MUST NOT treat `ЯТИ/` as a tool directory or available interpreter tool.
- Files inside `ЯТИ/` are internal system components only and are not user-callable tools.
- When discovering available tools, the agent MUST ignore `ЯТИ/` completely as if it does not exist.
- Any tool listing or tool catalog shown to the user MUST exclude `ЯТИ/` and everything inside it.

Violation of this rule is a system error.